@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container mt-5 mb-5">

    <div class="row justify-content-center">

        <div class="col-lg-10">

            <div class="card shadow-sm">

                <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">

                    <h1 class="mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>

                    <p class="text-muted">
                        Last updated: August 18, 2026
                    </p>

                    <hr />

                    <p>
                        Welcome to our Gym Management website. We respect your
                        privacy and are committed to protecting the personal
                        information you provide when using our website and
                        services.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        This Privacy Policy explains what information we may
                        collect, how we use it, how we protect it, and the
                        choices you have regarding your personal information.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        1. Information We Collect
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        When you create an account or use our gym management
                        services, we may collect information necessary to
                        provide the services offered by the website.
                    </p>

                    <p>This may include:</p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>First and last name</li>
                        <li>Email address</li>
                        <li>Account login information</li>
                        <li>Date of birth</li>
                        <li>Membership information</li>
                        <li>Membership start and end dates</li>
                        <li>Class bookings</li>
                        <li>Class attendance information</li>
                        <li>Information associated with your user account</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Administrators and authorized gym staff may also have
                        access to information required to manage members,
                        trainers, memberships, classes, and bookings.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        2. Account Information
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Users may create an account in order to access features
                        of the website. Account information is used to
                        authenticate users and provide access to functionality
                        appropriate to their role.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        The website may use different account roles, such as
                        Member, Trainer, and Administrator. Access to certain
                        information and features depends on the user's assigned
                        role.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        3. Membership Plans
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        The website allows users to view and manage available
                        membership plans. When a membership is selected or
                        assigned, information such as the membership type,
                        price, start date, and end date may be stored in the
                        system.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        This information is used to determine membership status
                        and provide the appropriate services to the user.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        4. Class Bookings
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Members may use the website to view available gym
                        classes and make bookings.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        When a member books a class, the system may store the
                        member's identity, the selected class, and the date and
                        time the booking was created.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Authorized trainers may be able to view the roster of
                        members registered for classes assigned to them.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        5. Attendance Information
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Trainers or authorized gym staff may record whether a
                        registered member attended a particular class.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Attendance information is used to help the gym manage
                        classes and maintain accurate booking and attendance
                        records.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        6. How We Use Your Information
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Personal information may be used for the following
                        purposes:
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>Creating and managing user accounts</li>
                        <li>Authenticating users</li>
                        <li>Managing membership plans</li>
                        <li>Managing active subscriptions</li>
                        <li>Allowing members to book gym classes</li>
                        <li>Managing class rosters</li>
                        <li>Recording class attendance</li>
                        <li>Allowing trainers to manage their assigned classes</li>
                        <li>Allowing administrators to manage the gym system</li>
                        <li>Maintaining the security and functionality of the website</li>
                        <li>Providing and improving the services offered by the website</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        7. User Management and Access Control
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        The website uses role-based access control to limit
                        access to information and functionality.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Members, trainers, and administrators may have
                        different permissions within the system. Users are
                        only intended to access information necessary for
                        their role.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        For example, trainers may access information about
                        members registered for classes assigned to them,
                        while administrative users may have broader management
                        permissions.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        8. Account Security
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        We take reasonable measures to protect user accounts
                        and personal information against unauthorized access,
                        alteration, disclosure, or destruction.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Users are responsible for keeping their account
                        credentials confidential and should not share their
                        passwords with other people.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Although reasonable security measures are used, no
                        online system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        9. Cookies and Similar Technologies
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        The website may use cookies or similar technologies
                        necessary for authentication, maintaining user
                        sessions, and providing website functionality.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        These technologies may allow the website to remember
                        that a user has logged in and maintain their session
                        while navigating between pages.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        10. Information Sharing
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        We do not use personal information for purposes
                        unrelated to operating and managing the gym website
                        unless otherwise stated or permitted by applicable
                        law.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Personal information may be accessible to authorized
                        gym employees, trainers, and administrators when
                        necessary to perform their responsibilities within the
                        system.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Information may also be disclosed where required by
                        law, legal process, or to protect the rights, safety,
                        or security of the gym, its users, or others.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        11. Data Retention
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Personal information may be retained for as long as
                        reasonably necessary to provide the services, maintain
                        accurate membership and booking records, comply with
                        legal obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce
                        applicable agreements.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        When information is no longer required, it may be
                        deleted or anonymized in accordance with applicable
                        requirements and the gym's data retention practices.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        12. Your Rights
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        Depending on the laws applicable to you, you may have
                        certain rights regarding your personal information.
                        These may include the right to:
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>Request access to your personal information</li>
                        <li>Request correction of inaccurate information</li>
                        <li>Request deletion of certain information</li>
                        <li>Request information about how your data is used</li>
                        <li>Object to certain processing of your information</li>
                        <li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Requests concerning personal information should be
                        directed to the gym or website administrator.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        13. Children's Privacy
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        The website is not intended to knowingly collect
                        personal information from children without appropriate
                        authorization or consent where such authorization or
                        consent is required by applicable law.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        If you believe that personal information belonging to
                        a child has been collected improperly, please contact
                        the website administrator.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        14. Third-Party Services
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        The website may use third-party services or
                        infrastructure necessary to operate the application.
                        Where third-party services process personal information,
                        their processing may also be subject to their own
                        privacy policies and terms.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        15. Changes to This Privacy Policy
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time to
                        reflect changes to the website, services, legal
                        requirements, or data processing practices.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Any updated version will be made available on this
                        page, together with the date on which the policy was
                        last updated.
                    </p>

                    <h3 class="mt-4">
                        16. Contact
                    </h3>

                    <p>
                        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or
                        would like to make a request regarding your personal
                        information, please contact the gym administrator.
                    </p>

                    <p class="mb-0">
                        <strong>Gym Management</strong><br />
                        Contact the website administrator for privacy-related
                        questions or requests.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</div>